# "property" in S1 means a person's right over his own person, while A1 and C mean ownership of an external thing. S1 is not one of the statements using the claim "property", so this is not a change of sense within that claim.
# Some readers find a shift in the passage from labour being "his" (P2) to his having an exclusive right to the thing (P4). But P4 joins two different claims, each in its own sense, so it is not a bridge.
